--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB PARITY (reproduced VERBATIM — cross-platform value parity, not a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Hook useApiLogStats -> GET /api-logs/stats (INTERVALS.STANDARD=30s). Go GetStats map keys:
  total_calls / error_count / error_rate / avg_duration_ms / last_24h.
  coreStats (4 tiles, exact web order + semantics):
    - Total Calls (24h) = fmtInt(last24h)                       icon bolt (web Zap)
    - Avg Response      = fmtNumber(avgDurationMs,1) unit "ms"   icon clock (web Clock)
    - Error Rate        = fmtNumber(errorRate,1) unit "%"        icon triangle (web AlertTriangle)
                          red + trend down + "High" iff errorRate > 5 ; flat (no label) iff >0 ; none iff 0
    - Errors            = fmtInt(errorCount)  red iff errorCount > 0   icon waveform (web Activity)
  Compact: big number fmtInt(last24h) + "Calls (24h)" + ("{fmtNumber(errorRate,1)}% errors" iff >5).
  isCompact = cols<=1 ; isWide = cols>=3 (grid 4-up) ; empty = "No API usage data".
  Decode note: last_24h does NOT round-trip through JSONDecoder.convertFromSnakeCase (folds to
  last24H, EMPIRICALLY verified) -> explicit CodingKeys are used (correctness, executed-green below).

